WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.680
We are in the middle 
of a big change.

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:06.800
Transportation, it’s going 
to be very different

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.920
from what we know now.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.640
When you build it, they will come.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.760
When you build the bike lanes,
micromobility will come.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.360
It will be revolutionary.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.680
And I think Israel

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.040
is in the front
of the revolution.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.560
Tel Aviv is very, very 
friendly for micromobility

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.280
which means the bicycle and 
e-bike and the e-scooter.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.680
It's a very flat city,

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.000
so it's very easy to bike here.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.520
Already we have 
170,000 biking a day.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:50.320
And from that 35,000 
are the shared scooter

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.800
and the rest is private.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.320
High tech transportation

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:57.240
is changing the face
of Tel Aviv, quite literally.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.880
The city is lined with bike lanes,
electric scooter spaces

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.120
and people walking all around.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.800
But it hasn't always been like this.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.280
When I started in transportation,
we decided to make a vision

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.560
how we look at it 
for the next 20 years.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.800
And the first thing was
to make a strategic plan

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.520
about sustainable transportation.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.920
How we look at that.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:23.480
Traffic congestion is 
the 2nd largest cause

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.960
 of worsening emissions in Israel.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.280
And Tel Aviv itself ranks as the

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.840
16th most congested 
city in the world.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.600
Which is why reducing pollutants

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.360
and creating 
transportation alternatives

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.120
has become a focal point
in the city’s strategy.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.160
All the city is rebuilding

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.760
so it will be suitable 
in the last mile

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.440
for public transportation
and micromobility.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.280
We made a map where we want the micromobility to be.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.000
Where do we want 
them to move?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.560
We rebuilt about 160 kilometers

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.800
of bike lanes.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.840
So micromobility and cars

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.160
can be mixed together
in the same street.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.080
We make more 
places for walkability.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.440
So there is street that we decide
that there is no entry for car

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:16.680
and it's open for more businesses
to open their chairs and tables.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.520
It's more comfortable
and more clean air

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.640
and less noisy.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.520
They used to say
that the best ideas

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.360
come in the shower.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.440
So for me, the best ideas come

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.440
when I ride in the boardwalk

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.160
from my house to Jaffa.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.600
To me, there is no reason why

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.240
in large, congested cities, 
people should use cars.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.600
Bird has literally 
transformed the city.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.320
In the past 4 years, we had 
over 10 million rides,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.760
over 550,000 unique users.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.920
If you walk around the city,
you see how many bike lanes

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.520
have been created
since we started to operate.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.120
In terms of the demographics,
everybody uses them.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.840
I'm riding scooters.
I'm riding bikes. 

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.320
I'm riding motorcycles.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.080
I ride just about 
everything that moves.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.960
The biggest concern 
is obviously safety.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.880
In the past 4 years, we've gone 
through an education process.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.200
Tel Aviv has had 
some of the earliest

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:27.960
and strongest 
scooter regulations,

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.240
like licenses being contingent on 

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.240
mandatory helmet use and 
operators being 18 or older.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.360
But they still cause accidents.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.720
It's raised a lot of questions
on what's needed

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.960
to keep people safe.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.160
We have to regulate the 
speed to maintain safety.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.240
More people wear helmets, 
ride in the right places,

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.360
and we need more enforcement.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.240
That's very important 
in cities like Tel Aviv

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:55.720
that have many 
people walking,

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.880
many cars driving.

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:05.880
Israelis, by their nature,
are early adopters

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.800
and they're innovators.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.640
There's a reason why Israel 
is called startup nation.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.960
So when they see a 
solution to a problem,

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.160
they go for it.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.040
This idea of a startup
nation is pretty prevalent

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.640
in Tel Aviv and it goes
beyond transportation.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.880
The city has been attracting
high tech workers for years.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.240
Over the past decade,
the number of startups

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.800
has reached 3,000.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.600
And the number of 
multinational research

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.000
and development centers

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.640
has tripled to 115.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.000
Tel Aviv attracts the 
very young people,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.240
people that work 
in high tech.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.640
We are a startup city and 
those are the community

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.360
 that like to bike.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:48.240
The vision of the city of 
Tel Aviv is remarkable.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.760
By 2025, the goal

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:54.200
is to have over 25% of rides

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.360
in Tel Aviv being 
by micromobility.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.760
That is unparalleled to any 
other place in the world.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.160
Whenever I see many 
e-scooters and bike riders,

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.400
I say, well those were
supposed to be

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.760
car drivers and they 
gave up the car

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.720
and they moved 
to the alternative.

